<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenia's SKB says lists GDRs in Munich.</title>
<headline>Slovenia's SKB says lists GDRs in Munich.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenia's second largest bank SKB said on Friday its global depository receipts are now also listed on the second section of the Munich stock exchange after being listed in London earlier this week.</p>
<p>On Wednesday the bank's GDRs, which represent 29 percent of SKB's equity, started trading on the SEAQ system of the London Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>LSE admitted a total of 1.3 million GDRs representing 65,000 ordinary shares. A total of $17.0 million was raised with the issue.</p>
<p>SKB is the first Slovenian company to be listed abroad. -- Marja Novak, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
